cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MalValid in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: MalValid
abstract: >-
  MalValid is a pre-deployment reliability and security gate for malware-detection
  machine-learning models. It scans a submitted model file, loads it in a sandbox,
  runs a battery of tests on a hash-pinned evaluation corpus and returns a
  READY / CONDITIONAL / NOT_READY / BLOCKED verdict with a 0-100 score.
authors:
  - family-names: Agarwal
    given-names: Garvit
version: 0.1.0
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/garvit-agarwal-purdue/MalValid"
url: "https://github.com/garvit-agarwal-purdue/MalValid"
keywords:
  - malware detection
  - machine learning
  - model evaluation
  - security
  - deployment gate
